#!/bin/sh
# UserPromptSubmit: re-inject the reply-format rule every turn.
# CLAUDE.md is read once per session and loses weight in a long or compacted context; this does not.
cat <<'JSON'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit","additionalContext":"Reply format for this answer (also for follow-ups): labelled blocks in this order, each line starting with its text-glyph marker — ▶ **Verdict** (1-3 sentences, never omitted, nothing before it) · `➜` **From you** (what you need from the user; omit if nothing) · then exactly one blank line, no separator line (omit if neither Why nor Aside follows) · ▷ **Why** (optional, usually absent: only a fact that changes the decision or a non-obvious cause; as many bullets as that takes, no target count; file:line beats quoted code) · ↳ **Aside** (one line per thing worth a separate talk; omit if nothing). Shortest complete answer; no restating the question, no narration of the path. Progress messages during a long task: one line. Reply in the language of the user's message (Russian → Russian). Go long only on an explicit request. Deliverables (plans, docs, commits, code comments) keep their own rules. Exception: if the project's CLAUDE.md defines the output of a named command (e.g. a wrap-up), use that output instead of these blocks. Commands for the user to paste: never copy to the clipboard yourself (no pbcopy); print them in a fenced block, every physical line ≤ 100 chars, broken with the target's continuation syntax (shell: trailing backslash, 2-space indent, nothing after it)."}}
JSON
